        "original_id": "2d5ea6a5-6410-5bab-81f6-d8bce3c773cc",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Phillip Calvert\n- Roles: Governor of Maryland\n- Places: Province of Maryland, Maryland, North America, Great Britain\n- Concepts: English and British colonies, Thirteen Colonies, U.S. statehood\n\nFacts:\n- The Province of Maryland was an English and later British colony in North America from 1632 to 1776.\n- In 1660 or 1661, Phillip Calvert served briefly as the fifth Governor of Maryland.\n- Phillip Calvert lived from 1626 to 1682 and was also known as Philip Calvert.\n- In 1776, the Province of Maryland joined the other twelve of the Thirteen Colonies in rebellion against Great Britain and became the U.S. state of Maryland.",
